  "physicalIntent": "Eight subtly raised rounded-outline head caps above a near-flat lower plate. Rust, coating and plate body share the plate plane with restrained local photo detail. The lower support includes visible dark head-contact shadows; they do not become new raised rings. No RGB, head position, palette, source scale, layout or perimeter change.",
  "parameterBasis": {
    "planes": ".61 head / .54 plate with .57 edge floor gives subtle .07 nominal head lift; relative uncalibrated units, not measured displacement. Every head support sample must remain above plate/pigment samples.",
    "micro": ".004 limits full photo detail span to <=.008; reduces initial0..1 cragging and prevents broad oxide or green patches from becoming architecture.",
    "bevel": ".6 at256reference gives1.2masterpixel sigma at512. Restricted to existing head silhouette interfaces; no new raised perimeter frame."
  },
  "supportedPolicyLimit": "Existing layered wrapper supplies rounded-outline caps with smoothed edges and slight source detail, not calibrated hemispherical dome reconstruction. Actual neutral opposed lights must establish whether this modest physical representation is acceptable; do not call it measured domed-head geometry.",
  "revision": "V1 diagnostic lower tips extended into some head contact shadows. V2 insets the raised cap support within actual visible head silhouettes; preserves v1 proposal/views as planning history. No master/map was authored from v1.",
  "geometryBasis": "Separate actual source silhouettes measured around all eight generated heads. Lower mask is their complement split into explicit trapezoids; it does not create heads from scratch, move them or sample another texture. Polygon raster edges are mixed head/contact/plate pixels and must be reported honestly.",
  "sourceVerification": "Required genuine independent source/master-only proof; no PASS row fabricated.",
